course: dictionary
lesson: 7854
title: The radius: from the centre to the edge
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The radius is a straight line from the centre of a circle out to its edge. It is also the length of that line. Think of a pizza: the radius is the distance from the middle to the crust.
explain: The diameter goes all the way across the circle, through the centre. Two radiuses placed end to end make one diameter, so diameter = 2 × radius. If a circle has a radius of 5 cm, its diameter is 10 cm.
explain: Radius also means a distance all around a place. «Within a 5-mile radius» means everywhere up to 5 miles away, in every direction. The context tells you which meaning you need: a circle, a distance, or a bone.
explain: Radius has another meaning in the body. It is one of the two bones in the forearm, on the thumb side. The bone is named after the same idea, a line from the middle outwards.
fact: The radius is a line from the centre of a circle to its edge, and its length is also called the radius.
fact: Diameter = 2 × radius, so radius = diameter ÷ 2.
fact: Area of a circle = π × r × r, and circumference = 2 × π × r, where r is the radius.
fact: «Within a radius of» means within that distance in every direction.
fact: The inner core of the Earth is about 2,400 km across, a radius of about 1,200 km.
exercise: A circle has a radius of 4 cm. What is its diameter? | 2 cm | *8 cm | 4 cm | 16 cm
exercise: «Stay within a 5-mile radius of the school.» What does radius mean here? | The shape of the map | *The distance in every direction from the school, up to 5 miles | The number of schools in the area | The width of the road
exercise: Which bone is the radius? | *The bone on the thumb side of the forearm | A bone in the lower leg | The bone in the upper arm | The bone on the little-finger side of the forearm
test: A circle has a diameter of 18 cm. What is its radius? | 18 cm | *9 cm | 4.5 cm | 36 cm
test: Which statement about a circle's radius is true? | *It runs from the centre to the edge | It goes across the whole circle through the centre | It is always longer than the diameter | It is the same as the circumference
exam: A circle has a radius of 10 cm. Using π as 3, roughly how long is its circumference? | *60 cm | 30 cm | 20 cm | 100 cm
